description=edgR Quasi-Likelihood (QL) pipeline is an approach for identifying differentially expressed genes in bulk RNA-seq count data. This module provides a robust statistical framework that models overdispersion, where variance exceeds the mean, while accounting for gene-specific variability from both biological and technical sources. The QL pipeline is preferred for its rigorous and conservative error rate control, as it incorporates the uncertainty of dispersion estimation into downstream hypothesis testing using the quasi-likelihood F-test.
